0,Mangbetu people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mangbetu_people,Ethnomusicologists have also sought out the Mangbetu to make video and audio recordings of their music. [citation needed] The Mangbetu stood out to European colonists because of their elongated heads.,Mangbetu,Nilo-Saharan
1,Nilo-Saharan languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilo-Saharan_languages,"The Nilo-Saharan languages are a proposed linguistic family consisting of around 210 Native African languages spoken by somewhere around 70 million speakers, mainly in the upper parts of the Chari and Nile rivers, including historic Nubia, north of where the two tributaries of the Nile meet.",Mangbetu,Nilo-Saharan
2,"Mangbetu court music, Medje village, Congo (Democratic ...",https://www.si.edu/object/archives/components/sova-eepa-1973-001-ref22178,"During his trip to Congo (now Democratic Republic of Congo), Elisofon visited the Mangbetu people living in Medje village, southwest of Isiro. This photograph was taken when Eliot Elisofon was on assignment for National Geographic and traveled to Africa from March 17, 1970 to July 17, 1970.",Mangbetu,Nilo-Saharan
3,Amangbetu olya - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uBzKjDyCgXU,"Provided to YouTube by IDOLAmangbetu olya · Mangbetu MusiciansMusique du pays des Mangbetu: Anthology of Congolese Music, Vol. 3℗ Fonti MusicaliReleased on: ...",Mangbetu,Nilo-Saharan
4,"Musique du Pays des Mangbetu - Anthology of Congolese Music ...Mangbetu court music, Medje village, Congo (Democratic ...Mangbetu - Hartenberger World Musical Instrument CollectionMangbetu Musicians - Apple Music",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aR_YsBxy_-E,"Jul 27, 2024 · Musique des Salampasu: Anthology of Congolese Music, Vol. 4 Salampasu Musicians Album View full playlist ""One of the most prominent features of Mangbetu court music is its formal organization. The musicians and dancers of the court orchestra are an integral part of the court. As elsewhere in Africa, there is no word for music alone. Each dance can be immediately recognized by its characteristic rhythm. The Mangbetu tribes have been at war with their neighbors, the Zande since the 18th century. They continue to practice “lipombo” a binding of the head, wrapped so tightly during infancy that it creates a lifelong elongated form of the skull. Listen to music by Mangbetu Musicians on Apple Music. Find top songs and albums by Mangbetu Musicians including Likembe (Beyru Music), Nadubele and more.",Mangbetu,Nilo-Saharan
